What is and is not covered

The License covers the contents of this repository: the governance patterns,
protocol documents, packet schemas, runtime modules, validation harnesses, and
templates.

It does not grant rights to, and this repository does not contain, Joe Elder's
private records, professional or client work product, credentials, connector
identifiers, or any brain memory contents. Those live outside this repository by
design — see docs/PRIVACY_AND_DATA_BOUNDARIES.md.

Reusing the governance patterns

The reusable contribution here is the pattern set, not the roster: brain-locked
specialist isolation, fail-closed packet admission, one designated writer per
shared resource with lease-serialized mutation, shadow-to-active acceptance
gating, and provenance-verified capability absorption. These are documented in
docs/SPECIALIST_CORPS_PROTOCOL.md, docs/AGENT_COMMUNITY_PROTOCOL.md, and
docs/SPECIALIST_ACCEPTANCE_TESTS.md, and enforced by the tests in tests/.

See CITATION.cff for how to cite this work.
